(SECTION 1: PYTHON BACKEND CODE ANALYSIS (app.py)) Tj T*
T*
/F2 8.5 Tf 11 TL 0.01 0.52 0.78 rg (1. Flask App Initialization & ChoiceLoader (Lines 1-18)) Tj T*
/F2 8 Tf 10.5 TL 0.05 0.10 0.20 rg (Q1: Why did you use 'jinja2.ChoiceLoader' instead of standard Flask template lookup?) Tj T*
/F1 7.5 Tf 10 TL 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg
(Ans: Standard Flask only looks in a hardcoded 'templates/' subfolder. If the project is executed from different parent directories) Tj T*
(     or has index.html in the root, Jinja throws TemplateNotFound. ChoiceLoader chains FileSystemLoader([BASE_DIR/templates,) Tj T*
(     BASE_DIR, '.']), ensuring 100% template resolution across any directory structure.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 8.5 Tf 11 TL 0.01 0.52 0.78 rg (2. Gazetteer & Geocoding Logic (Lines 74-125)) Tj T*
/F2 8 Tf 10.5 TL 0.05 0.10 0.20 rg (Q2: How does the 'geocode_place(query)' function work and why is it resilient?) Tj T*
/F1 7.5 Tf 10 TL 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg
(Ans: It uses a 2-tier geocoding architecture: 1) In-memory NER_PLACES dictionary (33 pre-indexed Himalayan hubs like Tawang,) Tj T*
(     Bomdila, Shillong, Cherrapunji) with O(1) latency. 2) Fallback to OpenStreetMap Nominatim REST API if an unknown place is queried.) Tj T*
(     If both fail/timeout, it gracefully defaults to Guwahati Hub (26.1445, 91.7362), preventing server crashes.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 8.5 Tf 11 TL 0.01 0.52 0.78 rg (3. Open-Meteo Weather Telemetry (Lines 185-235)) Tj T*
/F2 8 Tf 10.5 TL 0.05 0.10 0.20 rg (Q3: Explain the 'get_8_states_weather()' function and how it classifies risk.) Tj T*
/F1 7.5 Tf 10 TL 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg
(Ans: It queries Open-Meteo NWP forecast API for all 8 state capital coordinates (current temp, rain, wind_speed, humidity).) Tj T*
(     WMO weather codes (0=Clear, 51-80=Rain, 95+=Thunderstorm) map to conditions. Risk is dynamically assigned: HIGH if) Tj T*
(     rain > 18mm or high landslide-prone zone (Arunachal), MEDIUM if rain > 5mm, else LOW. Offline fallbacks ensure continuous UI feed.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 8.5 Tf 11 TL 0.01 0.52 0.78 rg (4. Multi-Factor Risk Calculation Engine (Lines 237-242)) Tj T*
/F2 8 Tf 10.5 TL 0.05 0.10 0.20 rg (Q4: Explain the weights and formula in 'calculate_risk()'.) Tj T*
/F1 7.5 Tf 10 TL 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg
(Ans: Formula: Score = (0.30*Rain) + (0.25*Landslide) + (0.20*Road) + (0.10*Traffic) + (0.10*Historical) + (0.05*TravelTime).) Tj T*
(     Precipitation (0.30) and Landslide slope (0.25) have the highest weight because monsoonal rainfall on steep hills is the primary) Tj T*
(     trigger for road washouts in the North East. Thresholds: <=30: LOW, <=60: MEDIUM, <=80: HIGH, >80: CRITICAL.) Tj T*
